---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Open source STEM electronics kits">
  <p class="eyebrow">TinkeringTech / ScoutMakes</p>
  <h1>Open source electronics kits, built to be understood.</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    ScoutMakes is an open source electronics company dedicated to encouraging everyone, young and old, to learn
    engineering. Every kit is OSHWA-certified, CircuitPython-compatible, and ships with full design files.
  </p>

  <ul class="spec-list">
    <li><a href="/products/fm-radio-board">FM Radio Board — Qwiic/STEMMA I2C</a> — an I2C breakout for the RDA5807 FM chip.</li>
    <li><a href="/products/fm-radio-kit">FM Radio Kit with Bluetooth Control</a> — build and drive an FM radio over BLE.</li>
    <li><a href="/products/robot-kit">Robot Kit with Bluetooth Control</a> — a wheeled robot you control from your phone.</li>
    <li><a href="/products/drv5032-hall-sensor">DRV5032 Hall Effect Sensor Breakout</a> — an omnipolar magnet-presence sensor breakout.</li>
    <li><a href="/products/drv5011-hall-sensor">DRV5011 Digital-Latch Hall Effect Sensor Breakout</a> — a direction-sensing latch breakout for rotary/encoder builds.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    All of our kits are sold through distributor partners —
    <a href="https://www.adafruit.com/">Adafruit</a>,
    <a href="https://www.tindie.com/stores/tinkeringtech/">Tindie</a>,
    <a href="https://thepihut.com/">The Pi Hut</a>,
    <a href="https://www.mouser.com/">Mouser</a>, and
    <a href="https://www.crowdsupply.com/tinkeringtech/scoutmakes-bluetooth-fun">Crowd Supply</a>
    (which also carries the FM Radio + Robot Kit bundle) — and every design is open source on
    <a href="https://github.com/tinkeringtech/scoutmakes">GitHub</a>.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
